      "mergeID": "651ad82ca8dcfd09533ec4de",
      "mergedPostDetails": "There seems to be a bug with either the beta or the current version of VRC with the stream camera, where if you open up the stream camera and look at your VRC window (Which I use for recording/streaming) there is a line in the middle of the window where bloom effects are broken in two.\n\nReproducible Steps:\n\n1.  Apply -screen-width 1920 -screen-height 1080 (I would assume this would work with any resolution) as a launch option.\n\n2. Go to any world with bloom/post processing applied. (Example world provided below)\n\n3. Open your stream camera and point it at any object that has bloom emitting from it. \n\n4. Look at the VRC window, you will see a tear in the middle of the VRC window, tho not the camera itself. \n\nWorld in Example: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_e301eab6-1362-4c21-9d0d-5b9e136999ec\n\nVideo: https://imgur.com/a/zIz0QAF",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1351] \"Tear\" in window view with stream camera.",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
